## Scout Reconnaissance Report
{step:recon}

Before any test is written, resolve what each endpoint needs to be called:
1. Build the dependency table: endpoint | required input | source type (enum/const · existing entity · produced by earlier case · human-only) | source (code file:line · read-only endpoint + property path · preceding case) | verified value | notes.
2. Map DAG scenario step dependencies: identify fields extracted from Step N (e.g. model_id, version, token, job_id, claim_id) to be injected into Step N+1 request path, headers, or body.
3. Formulate 3-level resolution strategy for `prep.ts` (or `prep.sh`): Level 1 live query -> Level 2 on-demand provision -> Level 3 fallback seed from existing historical data.
4. **Prove every source live** with read-only calls (`GET`/`HEAD` only, using the gathered auth): paste the real value and the property that extracted it. Never POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE in reconnaissance.
5. Output the runtime resolution plan for `tests/api/prep.ts`: the ordered read-only calls + property extractions that resolve each input at suite runtime.
6. List explicitly what could NOT be resolved and must be supplied by a human (and why).

Strict compactness rule: Output compact Dependency Graph tables and minimal resolution snippets. Truncate sample values to 1 line. NEVER dump raw multi-line JSON or full code files. Keep output under 60 lines.

Do not modify any file.

